The finding says the effect on health service use is unknown because there are no studies. This falls within the question's scope: the scope covers whether care reaches people on time, such as visits and immunisation completion, and "health service use" overlaps with that. It is not excluded by any out-of-scope entry.

The next issue is whether it is material. A page answering whether the intervention improves care and health would be expected to say where the evidence is missing. The finding reports a gap on an outcome the question covers, and a reader could otherwise assume that outcome had been studied, so I treat it as material and state it.

