The finding is an unintended consequence: a participant withdrew because they felt the intervention compromised their undisclosed HIV status. The scope explicitly covers unintended consequences. It does touch on privacy, but it is reported as a harm to a participant, not as a study of data privacy and security of the systems. So it is not out of scope.

Whether it is material: it is a single-participant report, but it is a rare, serious unintended harm (disclosure risk, withdrawal from care) that bears directly on the question, which includes unintended consequences. A page that omitted all harms would mislead. I would state it with appropriate hedging.

