The finding is a call for more randomised trials of mobile phone messaging reminders, measuring attendance and cost-effectiveness. It concerns reminder messages on their own, and the scope excludes standalone reminders without digital tracking of the patient's care. It also mentions cost-effectiveness, which is excluded too. The most specific entry is the first one, about reminders used on their own.

The finding does not say the reminders were combined with tracking. It describes "mobile phone messaging reminders" as a standalone intervention, so it fits the standalone-reminder exclusion.

